  "result": {
    "summary": "The exact frozen Seed1 1M integrated policy completed eight independent fresh2500 legacy-observation-bridge generic-greedy Slumbot sessions. All 20000 raw hands passed model/runtime/terminal/token-chain replay and session-independence checks. The independent cohort scored -21.7592 bb/100, raw 95% CI [-44.2479,0.7295], session-t7 CI [-67.5696,24.0512], with 2/8 positive sessions.",
    "conclusion": "The same-SHA external point did not reproduce the encouraging fresh5k value and was 10.3317 bb/100 below the historical Standard10 point, though the raw CI still narrowly includes zero. The preregistered 100k gate failed. This is credible checkpoint-level external negative evidence and shows internal multi-anchor gains did not translate reliably to Slumbot at 1M; it is not a mechanism-level rejection of conflict-aware learned self-play, nor proof that the approximately 1M training scale is sufficient.",
    "decision": "DO_NOT_SCALE_SEED1_1M_SHA_TO_FRESH100K",
    "next_step": "Use the already-frozen same-lineage approximately2.1M checkpoint for one correct-contract fresh5k external slope adjudication, because the turning-point audit rejected monotone internal degradation and the 1M checkpoint external result is under-resolved. Scale that exact 2M SHA to fresh20k only under the same conservative admission gate; otherwise redirect training objectives rather than spend 100k on either frozen endpoint."
